  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you are tasked with designing a solution for exporting data from a Firestore collection to a BigQuery table. The export process must be fault-tolerant, efficient, and capable of handling large datasets. Which of the following options best meets these requirements?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Implement a Cloud Function triggered by Firestore events to export data from the Firestore collection and stream it to BigQuery.<br/>B. Set up a streaming Data Transfer Service (DTS) job to export data from Firestore to BigQuery.<br/>C. Configure a BigQuery scheduled query to copy data from Firestore to the BigQuery table.<br/>D. Use an Apache Beam pipeline with Cloud Dataflow to read data from Firestore, transform it if needed, and write it to the BigQuery table.",
